  "problem": "Martin surveyed some students in a school, asking them if they have cats or dogs at home. His findings are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.\n\n|  | Has a dog | Doesn't have a dog | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Has a cat | $6$ | $9$ | $15$ |\n| Doesn't have a cat | $10$ | $7$ | $17$ |\n| Totals | $16$ | $16$ | $32$ |\n\nEstimate the probability that a randomly chosen student in the school has either a cat or a dog but not both.",
